{
  "id": "ss.relic.shrink",
  "name": "Runt instar",
  "description": "One body drawn twice at two sizes: behind, the skin it shed — a pale casing with nothing left in it; in front and less than half as wide, the live body that walked away, dark chitin with a lit back. The ability is the size difference, so the two sit as one pair and nothing else on the shelf is a pair. Three earlier passes tried to say shed skin literally — a tear at the crown, a split down the back, segment bands across the belly — and read as a horseshoe, a wishbone, and an egg with motion lines. What survives is thickness alone: a thin pale wall around a dark middle reads hollow at 32px, and hollow-beside-solid is the whole sentence.",
